  "description": "Florida's 3rd Congressional District, covering parts of north-central Florida including Gainesville and surrounding rural areas, will hold its 2026 U.S. House election on November 3, 2026. Incumbent Republican Representative Kat Cammack, first elected in 2020, is seeking re-election. The Democratic primary is contested by multiple candidates including Tom Wells (the 2024 nominee), Seth Harp, George Hubac, and Troy Albers. The district has been reliably Republican in recent cycles, with Cammack winning by wide margins in 2022 and 2024. The August 18, 2026 primary will determine the Democratic and Republican nominees, while third-party and independent candidates will advance directly to the general election.",
